<title>USA: Texaco sees 2.5 pct oil demand growth in '97.</title>
<headline>Texaco sees 2.5 pct oil demand growth in '97.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc expects world oil demand to increase 2.5 percent in 1997, chief executive Peter Bijur told analysts on Wednesday at the company's annual meeting.</p>
<p>He said the expected volume growth of 1.8 million barrels per day next year would &quot;about match the volume gain in 1996.&quot;</p>
<p>Bijur said this projection is based on Texaco's expectations there will be a &quot;slight slowing&quot; in the U.S. economy offset by European growth in 1997.</p>
<p>He said Texaco sees Japanese economic growth slowing to two percent next year from three percent this year and Asian economic growth easing to 7.5 percent from 1996's eight percent.</p>
</text>
